        <description>
            The AEOS adaptive optics (AO)
            system is designed for compensated imaging of satellites in low Earth orbit.
            The AO system lessens the blurring effects of the Earth's atmosphere.
            
            There are two control loops associated with the adaptive optics system:
            1) a tip-tilt control loop, which is used to correct for atmospheric image
            motion and tracking errors of the 3.6-meter telescope
            2) a higher order wavefront correction loop, which corrects for all other
            optical aberrations.   
    
            The Visible Imager is made up of a camera which is a Pentamax 512 x 512 pixel
            CCD cooled detector array.  The maximum frame rate is slightly greater than
            4 Hz and the spectral range is 0.7 to 1.1µm.
        </description>
    </Instrument>
